# UI8PX

Language-neutral. Screens must not invent a second CSS system. Layout is
Tailwind utilities on kit primitives. `src/assets/styles/styles.css` keeps
tokens, document reset, `data-state` dialog, and reduced motion only.
Paths are relative to the `app/` package root.

## Do

- Space on an **8px grid**. Layout: 8 / 16 / 24 / 32. Controls may use 4px.
- Style bricks through **`variant` and `size`**. Extra layout is a short
  utility list (`flex`, `gap-4`, `p-6`, `bg-card`).
- Color and type live in semantic tokens (`bg-card`, `text-muted-foreground`).

## Do not

- Grow job-named CSS (`.chrome`, `.workspace-grid`) when a primitive +
  utilities can do it.
- Dump long class soups that fake another primitive.
- Use palette names (`bg-blue-500`) or raw hex in screens.

Kit recipes may emit utilities. That is the brick's job.

## CLI (`ui8px` 0.2.4)

Policy: `.ui8px/policy/`. The CLI reads `.html` / `.css`, not `.svelte`.
`scripts/ui8px-prepare.mjs` mirrors Svelte hosts into `.ui8px/scan/` first.

```text
bun run lint:ui8px
bun run validate:ui8px-aria
npx ui8px validate patterns .ui8px/scan
npx ui8px policy review
```

`.ui8px/policy/scopes.json`: `src/kit` is control scope; views, chrome, and
the app frame (`src/App.svelte`) are layout scope.
